 ## Commands
 
+### Local workflow refinements
+
+This checkout includes local changes to bridge 0.4.0: shared full/core server
+instructions for MCP/CLI-only operation and interface analysis, explicit-port
+failure without session redirection, post-split model ID reporting, and additional
+`find_hbonds` parameters: `restrict`, `salt_only`, `inter_submodel`,
+`make_pseudobonds`, and `log_details`. Setting `inter_model=False` now explicitly
+excludes cross-model H-bonds. Native `graphics silhouettes` is used for scene
+outlines. These changes have not been submitted upstream.
+
+For a count between two split chains without creating display objects, call
+`find_hbonds(target="#1.1/A & protein", restrict="#1.2/B & protein",
+inter_model=True, inter_submodel=True, make_pseudobonds=False, log_details=True,
+session_id=PORT)`, using the actual atomic model IDs and REST port. Generic
+contacts, salt bridges, and Coulombic surface potential require distinct
+interpretation; surface coloring is not a binding-energy measurement.
+
 Once installed, these commands are available inside the venv (or via `./.venv/bin/chimerax-mcp`):
 
 ```bash
