@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+"""Shared operating guidance returned during MCP initialization."""
+
+BRIDGE_INSTRUCTIONS = """Use MCP tools or documented CLI/API access; do not use Computer Use or GUI automation.
+Operate on the intended ChimeraX session and verify its models before changes.
+Respect view-only/no-export requests. For binding interfaces, consider hydrogen
+bonds, salt bridges, van der Waals contacts, and electrostatic interactions;
+these categories overlap and are not four independent energy measurements.
+Use current tool schemas and installed ChimeraX command documentation.
+If the current GUI has no REST endpoint, report that limitation or use a separate
+headless CLI computation for a calculation; do not operate the GUI to enable it.
+
+Pass session_id explicitly for an identified session. A failed explicit port
+does not auto-launch or redirect; re-check the session identity before continuing.
+GUI focus or a matching window title alone does not establish session identity.
+If a window becomes empty or changes unexpectedly, inspect sessions before
+reopening files or replaying a command sequence.
+
+Splitting chains creates new model IDs and may discard surfaces, electrostatic
+coloring, and visibility. Inspect the returned models, restore the requested
+representations using the new IDs, and fit the complex in view. Splitting does
+not mean translating chains apart. Do not repeat a completed split just because
+post-split inspection failed.
+
+Restrict interface calculations to the two intended protein selections. For
+split sibling models, enable interModel and interSubmodel for cross-model H-bonds.
+The find_hbonds salt_only option selects ChimeraX's charged-group H-bond subset;
+do not label all close charged pairs as confirmed salt bridges. Generic contacts
+include polar contacts and clashes; proximity alone does not measure attractive
+van der Waals energy. Coulombic surface coloring is approximate electrostatic
+potential, not a pairwise interaction or binding-energy calculation. State the
+selections, geometry/protonation assumptions, potential range and units. Do not
+invent residue pairs from surface colors. Use separate, named interaction layers
+for readable displays. Retain the user's chosen chains and representations.
+"""
